Author: asmithbot <asmithbot@proton.me>
Date:   Wed Nov 4 12:51:47 2026 +0000

    compiler: preserve updated borrowed fields through selected calls (#1604)
    
    * samples: select generic crash forwarding through Build rows
    
    Replace the selected_crash_formal target prefix with an exact boundary requirement and four ordinary forwarding implementations. The caller still supplies Reader evidence, and the boundary retains the same crash guard; the twin changes only the Reader guard from strict to inclusive.
    
    The nine-place row and saved-argument and permitted-outcome controls are selected for focused hosted validation. No compiler behavior or owner question is changed; the broader target migration remains open.
    
    * psi: trace the selected crash conditions that reject valid calls
    
    All nine crash-condition examples reject before execution on the fixed compiler base. Capture the public condition retained at one failing call beside the applied requirement, so the repair can distinguish a lost generic argument from a failure to read its constant value. This temporary diagnostic is enabled only in the work-branch pilot and will be removed before landing.
    
    The touched README now explains the input and crash condition before describing compiler internals.
    
    * psi: read checked integer constants in crash comparisons
    
    Crash checking treated a named constant as an unknown storage read, even after evaluation had produced its checked value. Read that completed value with its declared type through the existing constant reader, then use the ordinary comparison checks. Pending values and malformed or mismatched constant encodings still supply no value.
    
    This checkpoint also makes the temporary trace visible through the corpus gate. The earlier diagnostic run retained the source refusal but buffered the trace; no successful check or execution is claimed.
    
    * psi: preserve the crash conditions of each selected call
    
    Crash checking discarded the selected generic arguments and read the interface declaration again. Reader<Zero> therefore became Reader<Limit>, leaving a valid call unable to prove that its crash condition was false. Read the complete signature already retained for that source call, and derive its conditions and contract identity together once for both crash-summary consumers.
    
    Unused generic parameters no longer suppress checking a concrete signature condition; unsupported values still refuse through the same strict reader. A two-limit program and its invalid twin guard against confusing different applications of one interface. Full focused validation and removal of temporary tracing remain before landing.
    
    * psi: index call contracts by complete symbol coordinates
    
    Arena handles do not define an ordering. Keep both index and generation for the caller and state when sorting the retained call contracts, so lookup is ordered without merging distinct symbol versions.
    
    * psi: preserve public crash checks after choosing an implementation
    
    A rewritten call still owes the selected interface contract even when the chosen local body happens to return without crashing. Use the retained public target before considering a private body summary, in both the dependency graph and direct call checks.
    
    Requirement calls now require their own retained signature reference and matching source location. Two unit controls reject missing and cross-call records; a private-forwarding example and its invalid twin check that concrete implementation choice cannot erase the public condition. Temporary hosted ownership-test instrumentation remains until the candidate is validated.
    
    * psi: retain the link from public calls to their executable targets
    
    Calls with only crash conditions were omitted from the retained call records. Keep every selected requirement signature connected to its source call and executable target, including when requires and ensures are empty.
    
    A shared checked-data query now joins the public crash-check target with the executable target. Scalar call emission, cleanup checking, and quotient eligibility use that exact correspondence while retaining the callee contract identity checks; none reopens source or substitutes a private body for the public condition.
    
    * psi: use the call index and test executable contract binding
    
    Resolve the unique retained call through the existing caller index rather than scanning every call during emission. Missing and duplicate records still refuse.
    
    Four carrier tests cover a valid public-to-executable link and reject missing or conflicting records, wrong executable targets or entries, another public signature, and a mismatched ordinary commitment or report identity. The temporary pilot runs these and the two source-signature ownership tests in one build-slot hold.
    
    * psi: remove diagnostic scaffolding before final validation
    
    * psi: make the crash fact match example observe both branches
    
    * psi: preserve integer bounds through match results and call captures
    
    * psi: name the type of joined value observations
    
    * psi: clarify the argument snapshot rejection check
    
    * psi: finish argument copies using their receiving types
    
    * psi: record selected crash call checks and execution results
    
    * tests: record selected crash validation on integrated source
    
    * samples: select inline sum implementation through Build
    
    * tests: preserve supplier calls in the invalid sum example
    
    * tests: record inline sum migration outcomes
    
    * docs: name Build-owned selection for const-family examples
    
    * samples: select const-family forwarding through Build
    
    * tests: record generic forwarding execution results
    
    * docs: introduce the borrowed-view target selection example
    
    * samples: select borrowed-view helpers through Build
    
    * psi: follow stored references through borrowed records
    
    A caller can replace a reference inside a borrowed record and return the replacement. Read the inner pointer from completed caller storage so the returned value keeps the right backing. Forwarding a write-only outer pointer still requires no read of its contents.
    
    * psi: trace the missing returned-reference relation
    
    * test: check target refusals during native publication
    
    A program can pass source checking and still have no provider for the selected target. Match its authored publication refusal after normal review and checking, without launching it or counting it as an execution. Use the realized target's oracle, and retain execution expectations on targets with supply.
    
    * psi: compose the checked origins of returned references
    
    * build: require authored supply for provider selection
    
    * docs: record completed returned-reference observations
    
    * psi: keep checked reference views through return composition
    
    * build: name missing calling policy providers before execution
    
    * test: exercise selected returns from a caller-owned view
    
    * build: render missing provider identities without a concrete contract
    
    * psi: isolate a caller-owned view through selected returns
    
    * test: distinguish caller backing in selected view returns
    
    * psi: carry caller views through selected reference returns
    
    * psi: follow the descriptor captured before later writes
    
    * psi: read returned pointees at completed call entry
    
    * docs: state measured selected-call results and remaining failures
    
    * backend: expose mismatched returned reference metadata for diagnosis
    
    * psi: keep fixed input pointers across referent replacement
    
    * psi: preserve public return regions through forwarded calls
    
    * backend: retain captured entry references across writes
    
    * backend: show the exact unresolved return cleanup
    
    * build: include the published provider configuration
    
    * backend: retain references written into caller storage
    
    * psi: identify the missing call completion association
    
